    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 22 with a heavy focus on speed and favorable matchups, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84), our two premier starters today. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is poised to exploit a weak matchup against Senga, and given our organizational mandate to prioritize stolen bases, his 45% SB hold potential makes him an anchor for the lineup. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** receives a significant boost from a favorable wind forecast and a solid platoon edge against Singer, securing his status as a must-start. **Caleb Durbin** (69.66) and **Junior Caminero** (68.95) also project as strong contributors, as both benefit from highly advantageous SP matchups and stable spots in the batting order.\n\nWhile we remain confident in our top-tier plays, we are keeping a close watch on **Yordan Alvarez** (58.52); despite his elite xwOBA, he faces the toughest test of the day against Cease, resulting in a marginal score that just missed our strong threshold. **Carson Benge** (47.21) remains a volatile start today, hampered by a difficult platoon disadvantage against Shota Imanaga, which depressed his overall efficiency. Among our bench options, **Chase Meidroth** (41.46) was the closest to cracking the starting lineup, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench because his projection against Gavin Williams failed to surpass the reliable efficiency of our starters. We are currently navigating several roster vacancies due to the minor league status of **Rece Hinds** and **Zac Veen**, but the active core is well-positioned to capitalize on the day's favorable pitching matchups.",
